  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain chances remain limited through midweek, \naccompanied by near to below normal temperatures. The next best \nchance for precipitation arrives Wednesday night into Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nShortwave energy should cross the region on Tuesday bringing \ncloud cover, and a slight chance of isolated showers, that will \nreduce high temps and increase low temps. Dry conditions with \nbelow normal low temps will continue into Wednesday night. \n\nGlobal models are continuing to come into better agreement \nabout a low pressure system passing to the north of Maine \nWednesday night into Thursday, though there is still some \nuncertainty in the strength of the low. Global ensembles show \nprecipitation moving in from the west Wednesday night and \nexiting by late Thursday night. These ensembles show a \nwidespread rainfall of about 0.5 inches with some pockets of \nhigher totals, though these rainfall estimates could change as \nwe get closer to the event. Ensemble models also show increasing\nconsistency in gusty southerly winds from the LLJ Wednesday \nnight. This system will continue to be monitored for changes.",
